# Warmpawz Team Development Bible

This rule is the **authoritative guide** for Cursor agents helping team members work on personal feature branches. Follow it unless the user explicitly overrides a specific step.

**Related rules:** `branch-health.mdc` (personal dev branch + feature branches), `deployment.mdc` (deploy scripts), `git-cli.mdc` (git CLI).

---

## 1. Repository layout (what lives where)

| Area | Path | Purpose |
|------|------|---------|
| Admin UI | `apps/admin-web/` | Internal admin portal |
| Vendor UI | `apps/vendor-web/` | Vendor/seller portal |
| Customer UI | `apps/customer-web/` | Customer-facing web app |
| Backend API | `backend/lambda/` | Hono API on AWS Lambda |
| DB migrations | `db/migrations/` | Numbered, idempotent SQL files |
| Deploy scripts | `scripts/deploy-*.sh` | **Only** approved deploy path (no CDK) |
| Migration runners | `scripts/run-migration-rds-node.js` | Run one migration against AWS RDS |
| Prod reference | `prodscripts/PRODUCTION_CONFIG.md` | Prod S3, CloudFront, API URLs |

**Region:** `ap-south-1` for all AWS resources.

