## 5. Deploy from local → **dev**

Use **only** scripts in `scripts/`. **Do not use CDK** or manual S3 uploads.

On **Windows**, run bash scripts via **Git Bash** or **WSL**.

### Pre-deploy checklist (dev)

- [ ] Changes committed on feature branch (or user explicitly wants deploy from dirty tree — warn them)
- [ ] For API changes: `cd backend/lambda && npm run build` succeeds locally
- [ ] For UI changes: `npm run build` in the target app succeeds
- [ ] New migrations applied on dev RDS if backend depends on schema changes
- [ ] User confirmed which components to deploy (backend only vs one UI vs all)

### Backend (Lambda) → dev

```bash
./scripts/deploy-lambda-direct.sh
# Default function: warmpawz-dev-api-handler on https://z0b3obweb6.execute-api.ap-south-1.amazonaws.com
```

### Frontend → dev

```bash
./scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh
./scripts/deploy-vendor-web.sh
./scripts/deploy-customer-web.sh
```

Each script builds, injects dev runtime config, uploads to dev S3, and invalidates CloudFront.

### Typical dev deploy combos

```bash
# Backend + one UI
./scripts/deploy-lambda-direct.sh && ./scripts/deploy-customer-web.sh

# UI only (no API changes)
./scripts/deploy-admin-web.sh
```

### After dev deploy

- Hit the dev CloudFront URL or local `npm run dev:*` against dev API to smoke-test.
- Check CloudWatch logs for Lambda errors if API behavior changed.

