## 7. Safety guardrails (non-negotiable)

### Git & PR

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| Work on `feature/*` branches | Push directly to `develop`, `main`, or `prod` |
| PR to `develop` after review | Merge your own PR without approval |
| Commit only when asked | Commit secrets, `.env`, `.next/`, `node_modules/` |
| Pull/rebase from `develop` often | Force-push shared branches |

### Database

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| New numbered migration files | Edit old migration files already on dev/prod |
| Idempotent, additive SQL | `DROP`, `TRUNCATE`, bulk `DELETE` |
| Test on dev first | Run experimental SQL on prod |
| Commit migration before RDS apply | Run uncommitted schema changes on shared RDS |

### Deployment

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| Use `scripts/deploy-*.sh` | Use CDK, manual console edits, or random S3 uploads |
| Default to dev deploy | Deploy prod without explicit user request |
| Build before deploy | Deploy with known broken build |
| Match backend/UI deploy order (API before UI if contract changed) | Deploy UI that calls unreleased API endpoints |

### Code changes

| Do | Don't |
|----|-------|
| Minimal, focused diffs | Drive-by refactors, unrelated formatting |
| Follow existing app conventions | Introduce new frameworks without approval |
| Run linter on edited files | Disable hooks (`--no-verify`) unless user asks |
| Add tests when behavior is non-trivial | Add tests that only assert mocks |

### Secrets & credentials

- Never print, commit, or log AWS keys, DB passwords, JWT secrets, or Razorpay keys.
- UAT on dev: OTP `123456`; `UAT_MODE=true` on dev Lambda (see `deployment.mdc`).
- Do not store prod credentials in `.env.local`.

### When uncertain

- **Ask** before: prod deploy, prod migration, force push, deleting files, schema-breaking changes.
- **Prefer** dev API + feature branch PR over local prod access.
- **Stop** if a command fails twice — diagnose; do not retry destructive operations blindly.

